         <Description>The Hinode Solar Optical Telescope Filtergraph (SOT-FG) Level 0 FG (simple) FITS data product consists of uncalibrated, two-dimensional filtergram images. It is the product identified by DataCode FG, OBS_TYPE=&#039;FG (simple)&#039;, and GEN_ID=1, and is distinct from other SOT-FG products such as focus scans, magnetograms, and polarization sequences. Images are obtained with the Broadband Filter Imager (BFI; FITS INSTRUME=&#039;SOT/WB&#039;) and Narrowband Filter Imager (NFI; FITS INSTRUME=&#039;SOT/NB&#039;) in various passbands used to observe the solar photosphere and chromosphere. The Level 0 data retain detector-oriented images before scientific calibration. Image dimensions and angular pixel scales vary with observing settings, including subframing and binning; typical unbinned scales are approximately 0.05448 arcsec per pixel for BFI and 0.08 arcsec per pixel for NFI. The FITS header identifies the observing passband, detector, exposure, and image sampling.</Description>
